<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=telescope">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Science and discovery</p><h1 class="enc-title">Telescope</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1608">1608</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A telescope is an instrument for observing distant objects by the radiation they emit, absorb or reflect; the first known practical telescopes, refractors with glass lenses, were invented in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> at the beginning of the 17th century. The earliest record of one is a patent application of 1608 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middelburg">Middelburg</a> spectacle maker Hans Lipperhey, though the actual inventor is unknown. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galileo-galilei">Galileo</a> built his own version in 1609 and used it to observe celestial objects, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isaac-newton">Isaac Newton</a> built the first practical reflecting telescope in 1668.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/telescope.jpg" alt="Telescope" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rama · CC BY-SA 2.0 fr · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lunette_mg_2368.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1608</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Middelburg</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Hans Lipperhey · <a href="/empire/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>The actual inventor is unknown; Lipperhey’s patent application of 1608 is the earliest record of a telescope.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/eyeglasses">Eyeglasses<span>c. 1290</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/optical-telegraph">Optical telegraph<span>1792</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=telescope">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
